  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've added a $11.40 credit to the account for the missing salmon roll, Ken. You're verified as an authorized user on Mei's account.\n\n- **Why credit and not a refund:** The salmon roll cost $9.50. Because you're an authorized user, compensation has to go to the account as credit instead of back to the card. The credit is the item's price plus 20%.\n- **Where it is:** The credit is in Mei's account now, so the balance is $11.40. It'll be used on your next order.\n\nSorry again about the salmon roll. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks. Can you tell me why it can't go back to the card though? I'd rather have the money back on the card than sitting in credit."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand. Here's why: Mei is the account holder, and you're an authorized user on her account. Our policy only allows refunds to the card for the account holder. When an authorized user reports a problem, any compensation has to go to the account as credit. That's also why the credit is 20% more than the item's $9.50 price.\n\nThe $11.40 credit has already been added, and we can only compensate a problem once. So I can't swap it for a card refund now, even if Mei were to contact us. The credit doesn't expire and will be used automatically on your next order.\n\nIf you'd still like to talk to someone about it, I can pass this to a human specialist. They'd follow up within 24 hours, but I can't promise they'll make a different decision. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get it. The credit is fine, I'll just use it on the next order. No need to pass it to anyone. Thanks for sorting it out."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Ken! The $11.40 credit is ready for your next order. Enjoy the rest of your evening, and I hope your next sushi order arrives with everything in it."
  }
